WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.370
G P S and other global navigation satellite systems support drone position, navigation, automation, return-to-home, logs, metadata, and timing.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.681
These conveniences create operational dependencies that must be understood.

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.969
Jamming degrades or blocks reception.

00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:24.281
Spoofing attempts to mislead a receiver with deceptive information.

00:00:24.281 --> 00:00:33.133
Weak lock, drift, warnings, cue disagreement, impossible movement, or unexpected routing are indicators, not automatic proof.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:42.491
Environmental obstruction, reflected signals, compass interference, antenna problems, receiver faults, and software issues can produce similar symptoms.

00:00:42.491 --> 00:00:49.320
Compare map, visual, compass, telemetry, mode, and site context while preserving uncertainty.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:01:00.196
Plan defensively with preflight checks, visual references, manual-control readiness, conservative automation, abort criteria, emergency landing areas, and documented crew roles.

00:01:00.196 --> 00:01:05.507
When navigation is unreliable, protect people and recover early.

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:09.301
Never transmit interfering or deceptive signals.

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:17.648
Preserve logs and evidence, report through appropriate safety and regulatory channels, and coordinate qualified review.

00:01:17.648 --> 00:01:23.971
The goal is resilience and safe decision-making, not experimentation with interference.
